2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 14922, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Gu877PpUbALQChzq4QunWQ", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 14922, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Gu877PpUbALQChzq4QunWQ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18978, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **What went wrong:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. All three regions now run it, the service passes health checks, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001, \"checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0\". It records the failure, what I rolled back to and the improvement afterwards. The listed follow-up is to find out why v2.3.1 broke before deploying it again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TM2357WaWeq4xJwjKRkszD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01V5sLvsXvU1qvJd5Satvd53", "caller": {"type": "direct"